[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
A fresh Kontrol-ID installation uses safe defaults and remains disabled until
it is enabled at Services > Kontrol-ID. Existing settings are preserved during
upgrades. The package manager installs the standalone multithread Kontrol-ID
engine and its exclusive policy GUI, including their dependencies.

Kontrol-ID cannot coexist with the conventional Squid or E2Guardian GUI/engine
packages because they own the same listener and policy paths. Remove the
conflicting products before installing Kontrol-ID.

Transparent mode identifies Windows users by source IP and never challenges an
intercepted browser. Explicit proxy mode initially supports native
Kerberos/SPNEGO. Configure and validate AD membership or import an AES keytab
under Services > Kontrol-ID > Domain and Keytab before enabling it.

For transparent identity, generate an enrollment token under Status and
Enrollment and provision Windows endpoints before enforcement. Domain join
passwords are sent only to kinit over a pipe and are never stored in config.xml.

Runtime databases in /var/db/kontrol-identity and protected domain state in
/var/db/kontrol-id-domain are intentionally preserved when the package is
removed. The standalone service is disabled by the package deinstall hook.
EOM
}
